  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8d08522e-039e-47ca-bc0f-79996fdfb0ed",
    "name": "Accelsius Search API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "The WordPress search route returns a lightweight, uniform result object (id, title, url, type, subtype, _links) across every searchable type on the site — resource-library posts, pages and news items. At time of capture 192 objects were searchable. This is the cheapest way to resolve a title or URL to the numeric ID the other operations take.\n\nAccelsius publishes accelsius.com on WordPress (WP Engine origin, Cloudflare edge, MalCare firewall) with the WordPress core REST API enabled and anonymously readable. This is NOT a product API that Accelsius offers to customers — Accelsius manufactures two-phase direct-to-chip liquid-cooling hardware and ships no developer program, SDK or product API. It is the content API behind the company marketing site, captured for discovery purposes. Anonymous access is read-only: the `Allow` response header on every collection is `GET`, and write operations require WordPress cookie authentication with an X-WP-Nonce header or an Application Password, returning HTTP 401 to anonymous callers.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Accelsius\n Email: info@accelsius.com",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
